":"18:00"},{"open":"09:00","close":"18:00"},{"open":"09:00","close":"18:00"},{"open":"09:00","close":"18:00"},{"open":"09:00","close":"18:00"},{"open":"09:00","close":"18:00"}],"note":"Typical hours — check the official site"},"summary":"Haughmond Abbey is a ruined, medieval, Augustinian monastery a few miles from Shrewsbury, England. It was probably founded in the early 12th century and was closely associated with the FitzAlan family, who became Earls of Arundel, and some of their wealthier vassals and allies.","summarySource":"wikipedia","wikipediaTitle":"Haughmond Abbey","photo":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7e/HaughmondAbbey.jpg/1280px-HaughmondAbbey.jpg","thumb":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7e/HaughmondAbbey.jpg/500px-HaughmondAbbey.jpg","w":1200,"h":900,"author":"JohnArmagh","license":"Public domain","licenseUrl":"","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:HaughmondAbbey.jpg"}},{"id":"shrewsbury_ditherington_flax_mill","areaId":"shrewsbury","name":"Ditherington Flax Mill","category":"landmark","tags":["history","photo"],"location":{"lat":52.7195,"lng":-2.7432},"visitMinutes":45,"priceLevel":0,"photoSeed":"shrewsbury_ditherington_flax_mill","tickets":[],"signals":{"commonsDepicts":0,"commonsNearby":80,"wikiPageviews":323,"wikidataSitelinks":10,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-22"},"hashtags":["ditheringtonflaxmill","shrewsbury"],"bestLight":"morning","summary":"Shrewsbury Flaxmill Maltings, is a flax mill located in Ditherington, a suburb of Shrewsbury, England. It was the first iron-framed building in the world and has been described as \"the grandfather of skyscrapers\". The mill is five-storeys tall.","summarySource":"wikipedia","wikipediaTitle":"Shrewsbury Flaxmill Maltings","photo":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d1/Flaxmill-Maltings_west_side_in_snow%2C_December_2017.jpg/1280px-Flaxmill-Maltings_west_side_in_snow%2C_December_2017.jpg","thumb":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wi