ene-battlefield/?region=Shropshire","official":true}],"signals":{"commonsDepicts":2,"commonsNearby":82,"wikiPageviews":383,"wikidataSitelinks":3,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-22"},"hashtags":["stmarymagdaleneschurchbattlefield","shrewsbury"],"hours":{"week":[{"open":"09:00","close":"18:00"},{"open":"09:00","close":"18:00"},{"open":"09:00","close":"18:00"},{"open":"09:00","close":"18:00"},{"open":"09:00","close":"18:00"},{"open":"09:00","close":"18:00"},{"open":"09:00","close":"18:00"}],"note":"Typical hours — check the official site"},"summary":"St Mary Magdalene's Church is in the village of Battlefield, Shropshire, England, dedicated to Jesus' companion Mary Magdalene.","summarySource":"wikipedia","wikipediaTitle":"St Mary Magdalene's Church, Battlefield","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/b6/St._Mary_Magdalene%27s_Church%2C_Battlefield._-_geograph.org.uk_-_383039.jpg","thumb":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/b6/St._Mary_Magdalene%27s_Church%2C_Battlefield._-_geograph.org.uk_-_383039.jpg","w":1200,"h":900,"author":"Jeff Buck","license":"CC BY-SA 2.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/2.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:St._Mary_Magdalene%27s_Church,_Battlefield._-_geograph.org.uk_-_383039.jpg"}},{"id":"shrewsbury_welsh_bridge","areaId":"shrewsbury","name":"Welsh Bridge","category":"landmark","tags":["views","photo","sunset"],"location":{"lat":52.7102,"lng":-2.75809},"visitMinutes":30,"priceLevel":0,"photoSeed":"shrewsbury_welsh_bridge","tickets":[],"signals":{"commonsDepicts":1,"commonsNearby":215,"wikiPageviews":120,"wikidataSitelinks":3,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-22"},"hashtags":["welshbridge","shrewsbury"],"bestLight":"sunset","summary":"The Welsh Bridge is a masonry arch viaduct in the town of Shrewsbury, England, which crosses the River Severn. It connects Frankwell with the town centre. It is a Grade II* listed building. The bridge is located north-west of Shrewsbury whereas its \"sister